> I play graphical nethack on Mac OS X 10.3.

I assume you mean the Mac OS X Qt version, vs. the Carbon port for Mac
OS 8.1 and up. I also assume you mean vanilla game version 3.4.3, which
is the only one I've ever used.

> Is there any way to change the tileset? I just got a new monitor and
> the default tiles look...bad.

Yes. Your game version recognizes several configuration options that
let you specify the location and attributes of the tile set:

* tile_file
* tile_height
* tile_width

You can specify these options in the NETHACKOPTIONS environment
variable, or in the NetHack configuration file. Here's an example tile
configuration:

tile_file=~/NetHack/my_tiles.bmp,tile_height=32,tile_width=16

where 'tile_file' specifies the Unix-style path location of your tile
file, and 'tile_height' and 'tile_width' together specify the size (in
pixels) of each tile image within the tile file.

Once you have the tile file configured properly, you may want to dork
with the separate Qt-specific settings that control tile display. Let
me know if you need help with those.

